TGPO — Tracked-Gradient Policy Optimization

This release contains modified training code derived from the Apache-2.0
GDPO/verl snapshot used for the experiments:
  https://github.com/NVlabs/GDPO
  commit e1afebe4d118aa2b01ce7a28b76fa52c9da6eeec
The license distributed with that source snapshot is preserved in LICENSE
and in each runtime directory. Upstream copyright notices are retained.
TGPO adds projected temporal gradient tracking, gradient coordination,
tracker restoration, task configurations, and reproduction launchers.
The original verl project is https://github.com/volcengine/verl.

Mathematical grading and evaluation preparation also use PRIME components:
  https://github.com/PRIME-RL/PRIME
  commit 18ad596f08d487bb546d80d738d99ec697bd2e75
Their Apache-2.0 license is preserved at eval/LICENSE.PRIME.

The BFCL setup script fetches, rather than vendors, the official evaluator:
  https://github.com/ShishirPatil/gorilla
  commit ea13468e4423454d0c213704fb87cf7cb3990433
eval/bfcl contains the local adapter and patch used with that snapshot;
the upstream license is preserved at eval/bfcl/LICENSE.

Tool data and prompt conventions originate from ToolRL:
  https://github.com/qiancheng0/ToolRL
  commit 8cee13ec0ca72f0461da372a93a6fd8140dbb840
The downloader fetches data from the original repository.

Datasets, pretrained weights, and separately installed dependencies retain
their own licenses. This release does not redistribute those downloads.
